<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Wellness and Mindfulness – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 9th Grade (CEFR: A2.4)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Wellness and Mindfulness</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> The Benefits of Mindfulness</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Compose a personal diary entry. Interactive: Comment on peers' writing in various formats, including on paper and online.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write a diary entry about personal wellness activities, including details about mindfulness and exercise habits and their impact on daily tasks (e.g., "Every morning, I stretch and meditate for five minutes before school. It helps me stay focused and calm during lessons." "After soccer practice, I take time to reflect on my progress, which helps me feel more motivated.") Can comment on a peer's wellness routine entry (e.g., "I think you can add riding a bike to your routines.") Can give feedback on a peer's mindfulness routine description (e.g., "I loved your tips for mindfulness. Maybe you can add a note on how mindfulness helps with stress.").</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 35%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 50%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 15%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a picture of a calm person meditating and asks, "What do you see? What feelings does this image evoke?" Students quickly write down 3-5 keywords related to wellness, mindfulness, and healthy habits that come to mind. (e.g., relaxation, balance, focus, strength, exercise). This activates prior vocabulary and prepares them for writing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to brainstorm and list ideas for a personal wellness routine, writing key verbs and nouns on the board (e.g., "meditate daily," "boost energy," "improve mental well-being," "exercise regularly," "maintain flexibility"). The teacher also models the pronunciation of multisyllabic words like "mindfulness," "flexibility," and "resilience," emphasizing stress. Short vowel/long vowel minimal pairs are briefly practiced in context: "He *could* improve his routine if he *cooed* less at his phone." "Don't let the *soot* from the bonfire stop you from enjoying a healthy *suit* of clothes."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is a 'routine'?" (Expected answer: "It's a regular way of doing things.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What does it mean to 'boost' your energy?" (Expected answer: "To increase or improve your energy.")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Wellness and Mindfulness."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short, authentic personal diary entry (approx. 80-100 words) written by a teenager describing their wellness routine and how it impacts their day. The entry will incorporate present simple (for habits) and present continuous (for ongoing actions), collocations, and target vocabulary (e.g., "mindfulness," "exercise," "boost energy," "mental well-being," "flexibility," "focus").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>Example excerpt:</i> "Dear Diary, Today, I am really feeling the benefits of my morning routine. Every day, I stretch and meditate for fifteen minutes. This practice helps me maintain my mental well-being and boost my energy. I am currently focusing on improving my flexibility. After school, I often walk with my friends, which strengthens my body. Mindfulness has many benefits for my focus during lessons."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Engages in group discussions on wellness routines, contributing suggestions and solutions to promote mental and physical well-being. (This stage supports the input for students to later write and discuss).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students read the diary entry individually.
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What is the main topic of this diary entry?" (Students write a one-sentence answer.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students mark statements as true or false based on the text (e.g., "The writer exercises every day before school." "The writer is improving their strength.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Students match phrases describing wellness activities with their benefits from the text (e.g., "meditating" -> "helps maintain mental well-being").</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice using Present Continuous for ongoing actions ("I am practicing mindfulness."), Present Simple for general statements ("Mindfulness has many benefits."), and collocations with health-related verbs (e.g., "energy boost," "improve mental well-being"). Focus on target vocabulary: <i>wellness, mindfulness, exercise, energy, benefits, strength, flexibility, health, body, mental well-being, routine, practice, meditation, relaxation, nutrition, balance, endurance, resilience, focus, habit, boost, improve, strengthen, relax, meditate, exercise, promote, balance, enhance, maintain, walk, stretch, breathe, focus, hydrate, mental, physical, healthy, strong, flexible, mindful, energized, balanced, calm, peaceful.</i></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Cloze):</b> Students complete sentences from the model diary entry or similar sentences with appropriate target vocabulary (nouns, verbs, adjectives) and correct verb tense (Present Simple or Present Continuous). Example: "Every morning, I _______ (verb: stretch) for ten minutes to improve my _______ (noun: flexibility)." or "Currently, I _______ (verb: be + focus) on my _______ (noun: mental well-being)."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Sentence Expansion):</b> Students are given sentence starters and a list of target words (verbs, nouns, adjectives) to expand sentences about wellness routines. Example prompt: "I like to _______ because it _______." Students must use at least one present simple or continuous verb and one collocation. (e.g., "I like to *meditate* because it *helps me manage stress* and *boost* my *mental well-being*.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction (Peer Sentence Check):</b> In pairs, students exchange their completed sentences from activity 2. They check each other's sentences for correct grammar (Present Simple/Continuous), appropriate vocabulary, and use of collocations. They provide constructive feedback (e.g., "I think you can use 'promote' here instead of 'make'").</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">15-18 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Wellness and Mindfulness."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Students will compose a personal diary entry (80-100 words) about their own or an imagined wellness routine and its benefits. After writing, they will exchange their diary entries with a peer and provide written feedback.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Individual Writing (10 min):</b> Students individually write a diary entry. They should include:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least three wellness activities (e.g., exercise, meditation, healthy eating).</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Details about *when* they do them and *why* (their benefits).</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of Present Simple for routines and Present Continuous for ongoing efforts.</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Incorporate at least five target vocabulary words (nouns, verbs, adjectives) and two collocations.</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Pragmatic function: Sharing wellness practices (e.g., "I exercise three times a week to stay fit and focused.")</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Peer Feedback (5 min):</b> Students exchange their diary entries with a partner. Each student reads their partner's entry and writes two constructive comments/suggestions on the paper. (e.g., "I loved your tips for mindfulness. Maybe you can add a note on how mindfulness helps with stress." or "I think you can add riding a bike to your routines to promote endurance.") This fulfills the interactive writing outcome.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy and student self-reflection.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students' written diary entries and their peer feedback comments.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Observation & Peer Checklist):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity and Coherence:</b> Is the diary entry easy to understand? Are ideas well-organized?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Target Vocabulary:</b> Are at least 5 target vocabulary words used appropriately?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar Accuracy:</b> Correct use of Present Simple and Present Continuous (e.g., "I am practicing mindfulness.") and collocations (e.g., "energy boost").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Task Completion:</b> Does the entry describe personal wellness activities and their impact? Are comments constructive and relevant?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following on a small slip of paper:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one new word or phrase you used in your diary entry today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one thing you learned from giving or receiving feedback on your writing?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Student and Teacher reflection, and connection to the next lesson.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt (Journal entry or quick share):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did writing about your wellness routine help you think about your daily habits?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What aspect of mindfulness or wellness would you like to explore more?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> What worked well during the writing task and peer feedback? Were students able to use the target grammar and vocabulary effectively? Were the instructions clear for composing a diary entry and giving feedback? What adjustments or scaffolds might be needed for students who struggled with forming sentences or providing constructive comments?</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In the next lesson (Lesson 5: Mediation & Integration), students will consolidate their learning by creating a digital poster or presentation summarizing the benefits of mindfulness and various wellness routines, using the diary entries as a reference for ideas, and presenting their findings, incorporating their writing skills into a larger project.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">3-5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>